# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel
/supabase/.temp/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REAL SAVED LEAD PAGES — NEVER COMMIT
# These contain real people's personal data (GDPR/UK GDPR). They are kept
# locally for selector validation and golden-file tests only.
#
# DENY ALL .html BY DEFAULT, then re-allow ONLY the fabricated fixture
# directory. Name-based patterns were not enough — a real page saved as
# "bad list navigator .html" slipped past a "*Sales Navigator*" rule.
# No .html file is tracked in this repo, so a blanket deny costs nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.html
!tests/fixtures/html/
!tests/fixtures/html/**/*.html
# The extension's own popup markup. Authored by us, never a captured page.
# Narrow exception by exact path so the blanket deny still holds everywhere.
!extensions/ui/popup/popup.html

private/
**/real-pages/
*_files/

# scraper binaries and reverse-engineering artifacts
*.rar
*.exe
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Extension build output — regenerated by `npm run ext:build`
/extensions/dist/

# Extension store packages — regenerated by `npm run ext:package`
/extensions/packages/

# Generated store screenshots — regenerated by `npm run ext:assets`
/extensions/store-assets/
.probe-bundle.mjs

# Third-party repo cloned in for reference, with its own .git. Staging it
# commits a broken submodule pointer rather than the files.
/Scout/
types/database.tmp.ts

# graphify knowledge-graph output (generated dev tool data, never committed)
graphify-out/

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Staging DB credentials — NEVER COMMITTED.
# ⚠️ .staging-db-url embeds the password in the connection string. Listing
# .staging-db-password alone is not enough, and missing this one put the
# credential into a commit on 2026-09-04.
.staging-db-password
.staging-db-url
.env.staging
.env.*.local

# Impeccable — installed by `npx impeccable install`, not committed.
#
# It writes THREE copies of itself, one per detected harness, each ~14MB and
# each containing a platform-specific native executable:
#
#   .claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/darwin-arm64/impeccable  (Mach-O arm64)
#
# That is ~42MB of binary in a source repo, for a machine architecture the
# Ubuntu CI runners do not have. It is regenerable in seconds with
# `npx impeccable install`, so it is a tool, not a dependency.
#
# ⚠️ THE HOOKS IN .claude/settings.local.json ARE WRITTEN TO TOLERATE THIS.
# Each is guarded `[ ! -f <binary> ] || <binary> hook`, so on a clone without
# the binary they no-op instead of failing. Ignoring the payload is safe
# BECAUSE of that guard — remove the guard and this becomes a broken checkout.
.claude/skills/impeccable/
.agents/skills/impeccable/
.github/skills/impeccable/
.claude/agents/impeccable-*.md
.github/agents/
.github/hooks/

# Generated design-preview scratch (one-off harnesses written while iterating
# on UI). Not product source, and a `require()` in one of them made
# `npm run lint` exit non-zero — which gates CI. Also in eslint.config.mjs.
.codex-previews/
.codex/
